====================================================================================
LIMITATIONS & DEVIATIONS FROM PLAN
====================================================================================
- Historical-change classes exist only at 50 m buffer (per dataset description); analysis (e)
  uses 50 m buffer only. Δurban numeric was used as a continuous alternative at the
  per-species level.
- AgriForest pathway has only 9 species post-dedup → per-pathway species OLS for AgriForest
  was skipped (researcher-defined n < 10 threshold). Plot-level AgriForest GLM was retained
  but is low-power (n = 23 plot incidences in total).
- Pagel's λ and Blomberg K are non-significant and λ < 0.5 for ALL species traits, so PGLS
  was not used per researcher's rule. We report OLS as the species-level model.
  Note: the λ values for pathway-mean urban exposure traits are spurious (values are constant
  within each pathway → uninterpretable phylogenetic effect); they were excluded from
  inference.
- Species-level mean urban exposure was approximated by PATHWAY-mean urban exposure (the
  FILE 3 dataset does NOT have species × plot linking). This collapses most species-level
  urban variance into pathway clusters; we therefore interpret the OLS β as pathway-level
  effects consistent with the conclusion that pathway × urban is the dominant axis.
- ALR transform used n.unint as the reference denominator; results are interpreted relative
  to Unintentional. ILR / CLR would be alternative compositional frameworks but give
  mathematically equivalent qualitative conclusions for 3 components.
- The 'duplicated = TRUE' flag was applied exactly per researcher decision; 4 rows dropped.
  All 77 retained species have a Newick tip label (the original Opuntia hyphen problem was
  resolved using a robust Newick parser — Opuntia_ficus-indica is correctly present in the
  tree; the tree has 81 leaves, matching the 81 phylo.tip.label values in FILE 2).
- JSON description typo 'urban.1956.500m ... within a 50-meter radius' was ignored; column
  names used as authority. Sensitivity across 50/500/1000 m confirms sign-consistency of
  urban coefficients.